A||||12||daveml66||can't get my fan to kick on by itself||||4||
Z||000000||daveml66||12-09-2001||04:19 PM||||I replaced my temp. sensor on the block, my temp gauge seems to be working now but the electric fan on the radiator will not kick on unless i turn the a/c on. i let the car heat up past 240..  still nothing .. whats wrong???||||reg||4
Z||000001||My7Fieros||12-09-2001||04:25 PM||||Relay?||||reg||1
Z||000002||daveml66||12-09-2001||04:32 PM||||maybe..  where is the relay ??  one of those located under the hood?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-09-2001||04:40 PM||||Seeing that you fan comes on with the AC then your relay is ok - it might be the fan switch located in the engine. On the V6 it is located in the head by the thermostat housing. There are 2 temp sensors there a 1 wire and a 2 wire. Ground the wire from the 1 wire sensor and if your fan comes on then it's the switch. You can get a low temp switch from Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTDude||12-11-2001||08:39 AM||||Relay is ok if fan works with A/C.  Has to be the coolant fan sensor.  Look for a 1 wire sensor (green wire) with a black connector.  I'd put in a lower temp sensor from the Fiero Store or Rodney Dickman.<P>GTDude<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000005||Spiff||12-11-2001||11:54 AM||||I have the same problem. My fan won't turn on even when I turn the AC on. I replaced the relay and it still won't come on. Should I now change the fan switch? Any suggestions?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||12-11-2001||12:42 PM||||Spiff- check the fuse||||reg||1
Z||000007||stingant0||12-11-2001||02:45 PM||||I had the same problem--it is a fiero gremlin. I had to ground out the switch, but it will run and never shut off. Don't get a low temp thermostat, the car is made to run at a NORMAL OPERATING TEMPERATURE if you have a low thermostat then it will take longer to get there. This makes the computer compensate and make the car run richer. <P>I never fixed the problem, grounding out the green wire will make run but it is a drain on your battery...so what I do when it is not hot out side, I just turn the A/C on until the engine cools down.||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTDude||12-11-2001||09:56 PM||||Spif....check for voltage at the motor....if you have volts and check ground too....then tap on the motor with a screwdriver.  Lots of times they just lock up and need to be replaced.<P>GTDude||||reg||1
Z||000009||ToddAsh||12-11-2001||10:39 PM|||| Had the same problem.Just put the 180 thermostat and 185 fan switch in from Rodney.Just got back from a nice ride.Runs better than ever.Warmed up perfectly.Ran cooler.Let sit and idled until fan came on and temp came right down.THANKS RODNEY! Todd||||reg||1
Z||000010||Spiff||12-12-2001||12:51 AM||||Phil and GTDude<P>I will try to fix it tomorrow if it's not too cold outside.<P>thanks for the help.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_11.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||G-Nasty||12-13-2001||01:32 AM||||I've got a good fan motor I'll sell for 10 plus shipping. Get a low fan switch from Rodney $24-Install it by moving waterneck hose and moving plenum hose away: undo one end only so as to get fingers to unlock switch plug. You will have to install while engine is cold. Removing the switch takes some time but it is worth it-these engines get hot.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Spiff||12-13-2001||02:05 AM||||Phil all the fuse's are good.<P>GTDude used a big piece of wood. Sorry no screwdriver handy. Plus aren't they for drinking? Anyway the fan came on so now I have to get a new/used fan. <P>G-Nasty you have PM.<P>Thanks for the help everybody.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_12.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Spiff (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
